{
  "description": "E-E end to end: a `global` is visible for reading and for writing to every scope, including a deferred handler block, and each firing updates the one shared binding rather than a fresh per-invocation one — two delivered clicks leave `:score` at `2`. Each handler invocation gets a fresh block scope (spec/execution-model.md:377-379), so what makes the count accumulate is that `:score` is NOT born in that scope: the write reaches the visible root binding (spec/execution-model.md:483-486). The clicks are delivered by the harness's tick-scheduled `hostInput.events`, so the run is deterministic; measured, the same source under an empty host prints `0`, so the fixture would detect a delivery that never happens.",
